# Optional list of wildlife cameras.
#
# Copy this file to cameras.conf in the same directory and edit it. The sync
# program reads cameras.conf automatically, in addition to whatever it finds
# on the network by itself.
#
# One camera per line. Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.
#
#   NAME  HOST
#
# NAME is the directory the photos are copied into on the laptop.
# HOST is the mDNS name or IP address of the camera, optionally with a
# different ssh user in front of it.

# The Scout's name makes a friendlier directory than "wildlifecam2".
# alice     wildlifecam1.local
# ben       wildlifecam2.local

# A camera on a network where .local names do not work:
# creek     192.168.1.57

# A camera whose Pi uses a different login than the default:
# oldpi     pi@192.168.1.58

# A single field means "use the hostname as the directory name too":
# wildlifecam3.local